I've been thinking about the mobility aspect of having my own Internet
node, and, depending on how much I want to spend, there seem to be some
good ways to do it.

Currently, mobile Internet nodes are a major area of research. The main
problem is routing. How do packets 'find' a mobile node?

Until this is solved (I've been thinking of protocols to do it as well),
having a stationary node somewhere is probably the best course, with
a mobile set of subnodes or maybe just a modem connection. With the advent
of satellite telecom (a la Motorola's Iridium) will make connections of
this sort pretty feasible...

I want to put a node onto a boat, but I'll settle for a satellite uplink
from the middle of the Pacific...

